{
  "mn78:0.1": "Middle Discourses 78 ",
  "mn78:0.2": "With Uggāhamāna Samaṇamaṇḍikāputta ",
  "mn78:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn78:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn78:1.3": "Now at that time the wanderer Uggāhamāna Samaṇamaṇḍikāputta was residing together with around five hundred wanderers in Mallikā’s single-halled monastery for philosophical debates, hedged by pale-moon ebony trees. ",
  "mn78:2.1": "Then the chamberlain Pañcakaṅga left Sāvatthī in the middle of the day to see the Buddha. ",
  "mn78:2.2": "It occurred to him, ",
  "mn78:2.3": "“It’s the wrong time to see the Buddha, ",
  "mn78:2.4": "as he’s in retreat. ",
  "mn78:2.5": "And it’s the wrong time to see the esteemed mendicants, ",
  "mn78:2.6": "as they’re in retreat. ",
  "mn78:2.7": "Why don’t I go to Mallikā’s monastery to visit the wanderer Uggāhamāna?” ",
  "mn78:2.8": "So that’s what he did. ",
  "mn78:3.1": "Now at that time, Uggāhamāna was sitting together with a large assembly of wanderers making an uproar, a colossal racket. They engaged in all kinds of low talk, such as ",
  "mn78:3.2": "talk about kings, bandits, and chief ministers; talk about armies, threats, and wars; talk about food, drink, clothes, and beds; talk about garlands and fragrances; talk about family, vehicles, villages, towns, cities, and countries; talk about women and heroes; talk at the street market and the place for water 